{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc","id":998092,"title":"My Kung Fu Beats yours!: Do Vs Kalindo Vs etc..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T22:14:26-07:00","id":998092,"title":"My Kung Fu Beats yours!: Do Vs Kalindo Vs etc..","content":"So, i been trying to figure out which martial art of all WoD is the most powerful on the hands of an experimented user. from both Fluidity, Danger and Control of this. and also as a complete study of every single martial art of WoD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T23:32:45-07:00","id":998111,"title":"","content":"Part of the issue with any such comparison is that some are innately supernatural, and some can be performed by non-supernaturals. A Kailindo user will cream an acolyte Akashayana, because one's a Garou and one's a mortal that doesn't count as witness to magic and can learn Do.<br /> <br /> M20 Do probably wins in terms of how big of a boost it is from the normal fighting abilities of basic combat Abilities and discounting the natural advantages of each supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:23:58-07:00","id":998905,"title":"","content":"The combat maneuver Redirecting Fist in conjunction with the Broken Rhythm School (Do Version of Drunken Boxing) could surprise the Kailindo User.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:43:44-08:00","id":1002586,"title":"","content":"Admittedly I've only ever glanced at the Changeling and Mummy games, but from everything where I've looked at the combat systems Do is handily more effective than any other martial art, though perhaps not so much as to counterbalance a lesser martial art being used by an eight foot tall fanged &amp; clawed monster that has fast regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:56:42-08:00","id":1002590,"title":"","content":"I am voting for martial arts for everyone.<br /> Except the rules. They shouldn't get any.<br /> <br /> Move the Do and the other Special Brawl talents over into the story and give boni for good descriptions of how awesome you make your opponent regret he messed with you.<br /> Every MA has Dex+Brawl the better you are the more brawl you should have bought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:12:18-08:00","id":1002594,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that Brawl, Melee, Dodge should function abit like Linguistics. Each Level gives you a certain number of manuevers you know. Because there is no difference between refined training and brawling except the refined training might teach you shit that has no application in a real fight. Maybe you can buy extras with xp.<br /> <br /> Do can be pulled down to &quot;AKASHIC ROTES&quot; because giving them two ways to be magical martial artist is dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:30:39-08:00","id":1002602,"title":"","content":"Street Fighters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:31:54-08:00","id":1002604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1002594#post1002594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the opinion that Brawl, Melee, Dodge should function abit like Linguistics. Each Level gives you a certain number of manuevers you know. Because there is no difference between refined training and brawling except the refined training might teach you shit that has no application in a real fight. Maybe you can buy extras with xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodge is dead. LONG LIVE ATHLETICS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:48:05-08:00","id":1002629,"title":"","content":"When did we get into &quot;should all these extra fighting Abilities even exist,&quot; instead of which is the best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:32:26-08:00","id":1002662,"title":"","content":"Sorry, my bad.<br /> <br /> I think we need a few Assumptions.<br /> <br /> Equality demands that the practicioners are identical twins.<br /> Akashyana ash-tray-gazes-at-stars.<br /> He could use Kailindo, Do, and every other MA you can think of because of his snowflakedness.<br /> It would ve not fair if you'd have to follow the tenets and rules of the opponent, so only rules apply that keep it at a melee level.<br /> <br /> Obviously Pankration would win.<br /> Because if a mage practices a fighting style which is about being \u201call-powerful\u201c and doesn't care about being nice and fair every other style has a severe disadvantage.<br /> <br /> IMO at least because I can't back it with quotes because all MA in Mage are equal (except Do of course).<br /> But Do could not possibly win against a Pankrationist of equal might. Because it isn't only about winning.<br /> Pankration is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T18:59:20-08:00","id":1002741,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that works. Plenty of Akashics consider winning a fight once they get into it to be important, and the philosophy of recreation pankration isn't the same as having that mindset in action; also Do users are completely capable of using &quot;hard&quot; maneuvers that embody things like pankration. Do is extremely flexible and can be used to support lots of different approaches to fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T00:31:23-08:00","id":1002792,"title":"","content":"You compare a fictional supernatural MA with a modern day recreated one?<br /> <br /> My point was that if two mages of identical might fight each other. The Pankrationist has the edge over the Doist because the Doist has accumulated lots of stuff not directly useful in a brawl. Just because the tenets of Do say so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T04:03:08-08:00","id":1002823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1002792#post1002792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You compare a fictional supernatural MA with a modern day recreated one?<br /> <br /> My point was that if two mages of identical might fight each other. The Pankrationist has the edge over the Doist because the Doist has accumulated lots of stuff not directly useful in a brawl. Just because the tenets of Do say so.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, Do is the quintessential martial art. In addition to lots of stuff not directly useful in a brawl, Do practitioners learn martial arts + Do maneuvers. Plus the Do practitioner can <i>also</i> learn pankration or other martial arts in addition to Do.<br /> <br /> You're approaching this from the idea that the eight limbs are <i>distractions,</i> but they're not. They help <i>focus</i> but Do is still an extremely effective martial art. If you had two mages of identical might fight each other with pankration and Do, the Do practitioner is likely to win due to access to additional options in comparison to the pankration practitioner.<br /> <br /> Also, your first question is very strange because you started this particular part of the discussion by directly compared a fictional supernatural martial art with a modern day recreated one. You can't really call people out for doing the same thing you did and expect that to have much impact.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Do &gt; pankration. It's pretty obvious if you work from the Mage 20 rules that Do &gt; pretty much any martial art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T08:46:52-08:00","id":1002907,"title":"","content":"1. I didn't compare the recreational MA with Do. I wanted to point to the original Pankration.<br /> <br /> 2. RAW Do&gt;Pankration.<br /> But that shouldn't be the case. Why are Akashayana superior to every other Martial Arts practicioner. The Wu Lung, Warrior Shamans, Viking Verbenae, House Flambeau why are these inferiour in hand to hand combat? There is no good reason for that.<br /> <br /> 3.The eight limbs could be seen as a distraction, because mechanically they serve as a balancing factor (or a excuse for it, because enough of it falls under stuff I wanna have anyway).<br /> <br /> 4. The only good thing they did was the cap at 2 at chargen. At least assuming starting level characters it stands to reason that<br /> Pretty much any Martial Art &gt; Do.<br /> <br /> Pankration can start with 5 VS the 2 dots of the Doist. The options available to the Doist are not enough at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:45:19-08:00","id":1003107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1002907#post1002907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I didn't compare the recreational MA with Do. I wanted to point to the original Pankration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original pankration was the MMA of its day, with people tired of traditional boxing and wrestling wanting something more exciting. And being primarily a sport, it both had rules, and would not equate to having a large degree of the mentality taught in styles meant for real-world application. There was also military pankration, but it was treated as a back-up to fighting with regular weapons like modern military combat systems do today. Tales of the mental toughness of military pankration probably had far more to do with the fact anyone reduced to using it was already in a desperate situation and fighting for their life; not because the training system imparted some special degree of focus or mental toughness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why are Akashayana superior to every other Martial Arts practicioner. The Wu Lung, Warrior Shamans, Viking Verbenae, House Flambeau why are these inferiour in hand to hand combat? </div> </div> </div>Not really the point of the thread. And as one of my players learned very quickly when they thought about how Do &gt; MA or Brawl, they realized that they all suck against people with guns and range anyway. The reason Do was allowed to be awesome when nobody else gets awesome unarmed fighting stuff like that is a mixture of Orientalism and not really giving a shit because weapons and magic are head and shoulders better anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. The only good thing they did was the cap at 2 at chargen. At least assuming starting level characters it stands to reason that<br /> Pretty much any Martial Art &gt; Do.<br /> <br /> Pankration can start with 5 VS the 2 dots of the Doist. The options available to the Doist are not enough at this point. </div> </div> </div>It's not that simple. Going for a hard style grapple MA to represent pankration does mean you'll get 10 MA maneuvers to the Do 2's one Do maneuver and four MA maneuvers, but the Do user still gets a bunch of other benefits (like being able to block and deal lethal damage without spending a maneuver on both, -1 diff to all general moves, and being able to ignore the Ability and style requirements for their MA maneuver picks). Which moves each side picks, and other Abilities (esp. investment in Athletics) is going to matter a lot to this equation.<br /> <br /> If the pankration guy doesn't take anything to help with defenses, and they can't block lethal for it, they're going to lose (since they can't defend against the Do users lethal attacks, and the Do user can use Dodge to defend with a higher dice-pool if they take the right Maneuver).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:00:23-08:00","id":1003117,"title":"","content":"The Do user can <i>also</i> take Martial Arts 5 in addition to Do 2, so yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T19:15:28-08:00","id":1003200,"title":"","content":"Also, I'd just like to point out that comparing a Martial Arts 5 character to a Do 2 character is Moving The Goalposts. Of course a person is likely to outperform another if the fight is between a person one step above a rank amateur, versus <i>a Master who is among the foremost in the world</i>.<br /> <br /> Yes, a Do practitioner needs to invest more of their time into developing Eight Limb related abilities before they can advance their Do. So that does slow down the character's rate of development for their raw fighting prowess. But first, a lot of those abilities (Stealth, Meditation, Athletics, Esoterica, Melee, Survival, etc.) are ones that a character might study anyway, simply because of their raw utility. Many of which could heavily complicate a fight between a Do practitioner and a Pankration practitioner, especially if the latter did nothing <i>but</i> focus on their raw Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> And second, like I stated above, Moving the Goalposts. Pit a Do Master against a Pankration Master, and the former will mop the floor with the latter, because those extra requirements pay out with invaluable dividends. Dividends like the ability to use MA moves the Pankration user can neither use nor readily expect, make attacks more easily, and inflict barehanded lethal damage. Hell, that last one alone would give a Pankration Master a run for their money, even against a &quot;mere&quot; Do 2 disciple. Try shrugging off bone-breaking strikes without the ability to soak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T00:40:32-08:00","id":1003276,"title":"","content":"Alright I surrender, mechanically Do is the MA to go for.<br /> But I don't give one feet of ground in the non-mechanical side.<br /> <br /> Just another pair of nitpicks, dealing lethal and avoiding such attacks are a common feat of the other MA as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T02:38:36-08:00","id":1003298,"title":"","content":"Your &quot;non-mechanical side&quot; argument boils down to assuming that pankration has the magical properties of turning people into crazy super-fighters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T05:24:03-08:00","id":1003335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1003298#post1003298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your &amp;quot;non-mechanical side&amp;quot; argument boils down to assuming that pankration has the magical properties of turning people into crazy super-fighters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am satisfied if there is an even footing.<br /> I don't see why Do should trump any other MA if the opponent is their identical twin.<br /> Consider this:<br /> Liu Cheng and Liu Bai grow up separated. They are twin brothers growing up in exactly the same way, but one: Liu Bai learns Do.<br /> Liu Cheng only learns Kung Fu.<br /> They have exactly the same amount of training, the same dots on their sheet, and the same Mentor.<br /> <br /> By the rules Liu Bai wins against Liu Cheng most of the time.<br /> <br /> But logically they should be evenly matched.<br /> Because the things that Doists can do, should be available to MA practicing mages. Or alternatively to every other MA practicioner, ig you prefer.<br /> I HATE the snowflakedness of Do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:50:31-08:00","id":1003516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1003335#post1003335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why Do should trump any other MA if the opponent is their identical twin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Do is supposed to be the best Martial Art. It's the platonic idea of Martial Arts that all other styles are a shadow of. You can not like that all you want as being a thing - and it's simple enough to house rule that out of the game I and think you'd be right to do it because I actually think Mage's ability bloat adds nothing esp. with clearly superior choices - but the non-mechanical aspect is solidly explained in game. Do &gt; Brawl/MA the same way Firearms &gt; Brawl/MA, because that's the nature of the setting.<br /> <br /> The twins shouldn't be evenly matched one is learning a mundane fighting style, and the other is learning a magically awesome fighting style. It's really just that simple. There's no &quot;logically equal&quot; here, because that only works if MA and Do are actually equal. They're not. Brawl loses to Melee despite &quot;twins&quot; because Brawl can't block lethal weapons, parry lets you defend with Melee and hurt your attacker, etc. Brawl simply isn't equal to Melee in the same way MA isn't equal to Do.<br /> <br /> I completely agree with the argument that it's not good for the game that this is the way the setting is handled, but that's not the point of the thread. As far as I'm concerned a huge number of the Abilities (esp. ones like Do or High Rituals) should just standard Abilities that get a bonus from Esoterica since Esoterica basically exists to let your Focus give you some boosts to mundane actions. Esoterica (Do) + Brawl would trump Brawl, but it would have the associated cost of investing in Esoterica, and combat mages of all stripes could access similar things.<br /> <br /> But how we might like things done doesn't change how things are in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:40:46-08:00","id":1003612,"title":"","content":"Firearms and Melee are useless without their tools of the trade. They are better because they bring something extra.<br /> <br /> A magically awesome fighting style is fine if a unawakened learns it. But a mage can make Brawl magically awesome.<br /> <br /> I like your Esoterica idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1003516#post1003516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how we might like things done doesn't change how things are in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are mages, we change the game constantly. <br /> If you assemble a new group, how much time is needed before everyone is on the same level, on average?<br /> People often use HR without knowing.<br /> Sometimes they state something RAW is a HR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T20:11:29-08:00","id":1003759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1003335#post1003335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why Do should trump any other MA if the opponent is their identical twin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Honestly....im pretty tired as i read this and for A Single moment i thought about Donald Trump doing Do","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T04:03:14-08:00","id":1005297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/998092-my-kung-fu-beats-yours-do-vs-kalindo-vs-etc?p=1003516#post1003516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Brawl loses to Melee despite &amp;quot;twins&amp;quot; because Brawl can't block lethal weapons,</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how durable the character is, or if they're wearing armor. An elder gangrel or a werewolf could do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:08:49-08:00","id":1005489,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's got pretty much zero to do with the point though.<br /> <br /> The question isn't, &quot;can supernatural powers make up for the deficiencies in a given combat Ability,&quot; but how the different Abilities rack up against each other. Yes, there are supernatural stuff that can make Brawl better, but there's also supernatural stuff that can make Melee and Firearms better too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}